        <body>
            <div xml:id="d248">

                <pb facs="0332" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg250"/>

                <head>Mr. Portman to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 32.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Yedo,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 9, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith, No.
                    1, translation of a letter from the minister of foreign affairs, informing me of
                    the departure, this day, of the Tycoon, for the purpose of placing himself at
                    the head of his army, which is to suppress the rebellion of the Prince of
                    Choshu.</p>
                <p>This army is to gather contingent forces from various Daimios on the way, and, on
                    arrival on the scene of action, it is estimated, will fully muster one hundred
                    thousand fighting men.</p>
                <p>There appears to be much uncertainty in regard to the attitude of several Daimios
                    in the vicinity of Nagato, whose position as yet is not sufficiently defined;
                    but there appears, also, to prevail an impression that the presence of so large
                    a force will, by itself, be found sufficient to overawe not only the Prince of
                    Choshu, but also such other Daimios who are now more or less wavering in their
                    allegiance, and that the solution of all internal difficulties is now near at an
                    end.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. L. C. PORTMAN, <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé d’ Affaires ad interim
                            in Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d248-a1.xml" xpointer="d248-a1"/>
